# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc, ln(), asin(), acos(), acosh(). An MPFR real (Digits > 14) meets a double: ln of a negative _REAL returns log(-x)+cst_pi*cst_i, and the symbolic pi met the MPFR value as a double, so ln(-pi), sqrt(-pi) and every inverse function that goes through ln of a negative real (asin(e) at Digits 30: 1.5707963267949-1.6574544541531*i) printed 14 digits. Complex acos returns cst_pi/2-asinasln(z) with the same double pi/2 (evalf(acos(1+i),30): real part 0.904556894302377..., mpmath 0.904556894302381...). asin and acos of an MPFR real outside [-1,1], and acosh of one below 1, call MPFR (NaN, so undef), where the _FLOAT_ branch already takes the ln form. Uses m_pi at the argument's precision in ln and acos, and the ln forms (the principal branches) outside the real domains. Doubles and exact arguments are unchanged.
